    title: "Apple 終止 iPhone 升級計畫，推出 Apple Upgrade 取代，改變用戶設備購買與租賃模式",
    summary: "Apple 宣布正式啟動新的 Apple Upgrade 租賃計畫，涵蓋 iPhone、iPad、Apple Watch 和 Mac。與此同時，Apple 也正式終止了原有的 iPhone Upgrade Program。對於現有參與 iPhone Upgrade Program 的用戶，在達到升級資格時，將無法再透過舊計畫獲得新 iPhone。取而代之的是，用戶必須選擇新的購買方式，包括透過 Apple Upgrade 租賃新設備、使用 Apple Card 月分期付款、直接購買產品，或選擇電信商融資。文章指出，舊的 iPhone Upgrade Program 是一種由 Citizens One 支持的分期貸款，款項用於支付購買價格；而新的 Apple Upgrade 則是租賃模式，設備所有權屬於 Klarna，用戶的付款僅涵蓋設備的使用費用。此外，舊計畫將 AppleCare 涵蓋在月費內，而新系統則將其作為獨立的附加選項。這代表 Apple 改變了用戶設備的財務結構和所有權模式，讓用戶在升級時有更多元的選擇。",
    tags: ["Apple", "iPhone", "Apple Upgrade", "iPhone Upgrade Program", "租賃模式", "設備購買"],
    title_en: "Apple Discontinues iPhone Upgrade Program, Replaces It with Apple Upgrade, Changing User Device Purchase and Leasing Models",
    summary_en: "Apple has announced the official launch of a new Apple Upgrade leasing plan, covering iPhone, iPad, Apple Watch, and Mac. Concurrently, Apple has officially discontinued the original iPhone Upgrade Program. Users currently participating in the iPhone Upgrade Program will no longer be able to acquire a new iPhone through the old plan when they reach upgrade eligibility. Instead, users must choose from new purchasing methods, including leasing a new device through Apple Upgrade, using Apple Card installment payments, direct product purchase, or opting for carrier financing. The article points out that the old iPhone Upgrade Program was an installment loan supported by Citizens One, with funds used to pay for the purchase price; whereas the new Apple Upgrade is a leasing model, with device ownership belonging to Klarna, and the user's payments only covering the device usage fee. Furthermore, the old plan included AppleCare within the monthly fee, while the new system treats it as a separate add-on option. This signifies that Apple has changed the financial structure and ownership model of user devices, providing users with more diverse choices when upgrading.",
    tags_en: ["Apple", "iPhone", "Apple Upgrade", "iPhone Upgrade Program", "Leasing Model", "Device Purchase"],
