    summary_en: "According to supply chain sources, Apple is making significant changes to the display supply chain for the next-generation MacBook Ultra. Historically, Apple has typically collaborated with multiple suppliers to ensure display reliability and facilitate price negotiations. However, it is reported that Apple has decided to use only a single screen supplier. This decision may lead to an increase in manufacturing costs, further driving up the retail price of the MacBook Ultra. Although the article does not provide specific pricing or technical details, this highlights the significant impact of supply chain strategy on the pricing of high-end products, requiring consumers and industry observers to monitor Apple's future dynamics in component sourcing and product positioning.",
