    summary: "為加強防禦暴力破解（brute-forcing）的風險，三星在 One UI 9（基於 Android 17）中大幅收緊了裝置解鎖的限制。相較於 Google Android 17 預設的限制，三星的政策更為嚴格。新的機制規定，當用戶連續失敗的解鎖嘗試達到 13 次時，Galaxy 裝置將會被永久鎖定，唯一的解鎖方式是執行恢復原廠設定（factory reset）。此外，One UI 9 還實施了更嚴格的計數機制：失敗次數越多，每次鎖定後的等待時間將會呈指數級增加。系統會在鎖定畫面明確顯示剩餘的嘗試次數，讓用戶清楚了解裝置的安全性狀態。此更新目前已在 Galaxy Z Fold 8 上推出，並將在未來幾個月內擴展至其他 Galaxy 裝置。",
    tags: ["Samsung", "One UI 9", "Android 17", "裝置鎖定", "暴力破解", "Galaxy Z Fold 8"],
    title_en: "Samsung One UI 9 Strengthens Device Lock Mechanisms: Failed Unlock Attempts Limit Raised to 13, Triggering Permanent Lockout",
    summary_en: "To enhance defense against brute-forcing risks, Samsung has significantly tightened device unlock restrictions in One UI 9 (based on Android 17). Samsung's policy is stricter compared to the default limits set by Google Android 17. The new mechanism stipulates that if a user reaches 13 consecutive failed unlock attempts, the Galaxy device will be permanently locked, with the only method of unlocking being a factory reset. Furthermore, One UI 9 implements a stricter counting mechanism: the longer the failed attempts, the exponentially longer the waiting time after each lock. The system will clearly display the remaining attempts on the lock screen, allowing users to understand the device's security status. This update has been rolled out on the Galaxy Z Fold 8 and will be expanded to other Galaxy devices in the coming months.",
    tags_en: ["Samsung", "One UI 9", "Android 17", "Device Lock", "Brute-forcing", "Galaxy Z Fold 8"],
