    title_en: "Microsoft Releases MDASH System Integrating MAI-Cyber-1-Flash to Enhance Cybersecurity Capabilities",
    summary_en: "Microsoft announced the launch of MAI-Cyber-1-Flash, a dedicated cybersecurity model, within its MDASH system. This system aims to enhance vulnerability identification and remediation capabilities through multi-model combination. MAI-Cyber-1-Flash is a Sparse Mixture-of-Experts Transformer with 137 billion total parameters, capable of handling up to 90% of MDASH tasks, reserving GPT-5.4 for the most challenging 10% of tasks. Microsoft claims that with this configuration, the system achieved a high score of 95.95% in CyberGym testing and reports a 50% reduction in cost compared to its current best configuration. The system is currently limited to the private preview stage of Azure AI Foundry and serves as the first use case for the broader defensive security agent system, Project Perception. Users should note that the model and system test results were obtained in an isolated environment, and the generated code and text may be inaccurate, requiring careful review.",
