    title_en: "Gemini App Updates Interface and Notification Settings: Simplifying Thought Mode Selection and Enhancing Task Management",
    summary_en: "Google's Gemini application is undergoing interface optimization and feature updates. Regarding model selection, the previous two-step process of setting 'Standard' and 'Extended Thought' via a dropdown menu has been simplified to a single step, directly displaying the 'Extended Thought' mode. This change has been widely rolled out on both Android and web platforms. Furthermore, the Gemini Spark interface on Android has been adjusted. Related tasks (such as 'All', 'Scheduled', 'Needs Input', etc.) have been moved from old menu buttons to the top tab bar, and the old menu buttons have been replaced with a magnifying glass icon for 'Search Tasks'. More importantly, the Gemini App on Android has added notification control functionality. Users can now independently control notifications for four categories: 'Daily Summary', 'Scheduled Actions', 'Replies', and 'Product Updates and Alerts'. This helps users choose whether they want to receive alert reminders or simply view the content when they open the application. These notification settings are not yet fully available, but when they are, they can be found in the account menu.",
